Manager method Does <code>createMenu(string $name)</code> Creates an empty menu called <code>$name</code> and returns the manager. Replaces a menu that has the same name, so never call it for <code>sidebar</code>. <code>menu(string $name)</code> The menu called <code>$name</code>, created if it doesn't exist. <p>The Admin theme only renders <code>sidebar</code>, so you render a custom menu yourself. Build it in <code>initAdmin()</code>:</p> <pre><code>$reports = service('menus')-&gt;menu('reports');

$reports-&gt;collect('sales', [
    new MenuItem(['title' =&gt; 'By month', 'namedRoute' =&gt; 'reports-monthly', 'permission' =&gt; 'reports.view']),
    new MenuItem(['title' =&gt; 'By region', 'namedRoute' =&gt; 'reports-region', 'permission' =&gt; 'reports.view']),
]);
</code></pre> <p>Then loop over it in a view:</p> <pre><code>&lt;?php $reports = service('menus')-&gt;menu('reports') ?&gt;
&lt;?php foreach ($reports-&gt;collections() as $collection) : ?&gt;
    &lt;?php if (! $collection-&gt;hasVisibleItems()) {
        continue;
    } ?&gt;
    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;?= esc($collection-&gt;title) ?&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;?php foreach ($collection-&gt;items() as $item) : ?&gt;
        &lt;?php if ($item-&gt;userCanSee()) : ?&gt;
            &lt;a href="&lt;?= site_url($item-&gt;url) ?&gt;" &lt;?= $item === $reports-&gt;activeItem() ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' ?&gt;&gt;
                &lt;?= $item-&gt;icon ?&gt; &lt;?= esc($item-&gt;title) ?&gt;
            &lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;?php endif ?&gt;
    &lt;?php endforeach ?&gt;
&lt;?php endforeach ?&gt;
</code></pre>
